  "body": "Independently corroborates the local complementary-block inverse argument in `research/kappa-nine/MIXED-RANK-TEST.md`. The source already has a valid Schur proof; this adds an explicit kernel-isomorphism proof of the classical nullity identity and source-bound executable evidence, with no correction or new-theorem claim.\n\nThe literal six-by-six rational example passes all 4,096 rectangular subblock checks and 10,240 kernel-basis transports, recovering its block ranks 2,4,2,4 and regular rank-one restrictions. A separate adjugate/minor engine exhausts all 11,232 matrices of GL(3,F3), checking 404,352 proper block pairs. Full histograms and deterministic traces bind both receipts. Eight mathematical and five package controls pass with assertions disabled.\n\nOnly `research/complementary-nullity-audit75/` is added. Original source/receipt/credit and frozen selected context are pinned at `2921874911956718fcaaaf9396fe8267b3cfa9f0`. Optimized package replay, selected-result verification and whitespace checks passed. Native/full supplier, hosted CI and Lean were not run. No new Fano exclusion, supplier or kappa is claimed; surviving branches remain open.\n\nCredit: Douglas Colkitt's original kappa-nine application and disclosed OpenAI Codex assistance. Audit contributor @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n",
